// §3.2 corrections from claude/sds-pages-concept.md applied:
//   (1) NO ACGIH TLV anywhere (copyright DROP list) — §8 ships NIOSH REL instead, at import.
//   (2) All mockup numbers were placeholders — every value below comes from the DB (D10).
//   (3) "Full substance report →" button lives in the TOOL, not on this page.
//   (4) Emergency button copy TBD — whole button gated behind EMERGENCY_ENABLED (v1.5, ERG import).
//
// ROLE (Sergej, 2026-07-27): this page is NOT an SDS and NOT a PDF. It is an
// SDS-style substance report that collects organic traffic and routes it:
//   -> our tools (storage verdict / future emergency mode)
//   -> SDS Manager (for real SDS management)  -> supplier PDFs (official docs)
//   -> compliance hub + primary sources.
// Sections mirror the 16-section SDS convention (chemists search "sds section 9").
// Sections render only when data exists — imports light them up with no code change:
//   §4/§5/§6      -> ✅ imported session 16 (substance_response, 99 substances, from
//                    cameo.sqlite 3.1.0). Every string is US-federal public domain:
//                    ERG 2024 (PHMSA) · NIOSH Pocket Guide (CDC) · CHRIS (USCG 1999) ·
//                    NTP 1992 · EPA 1998. Stored VERBATIM; the citation CAMEO appends
//                    inline was lifted into *_src so the page can attribute explicitly.
//                    These three sections render for variant B/C pages too — a substance
//                    with no Annex VI entry still has published response data.
//                    prot_clothing IS imported but deliberately NOT rendered: 9 of the
//                    USCG texts name a glove material, which the concept keeps out of
//                    scope. It waits for §8, where PPE belongs (Sergej, session 16).
//   §8 OEL        -> Step-3 import (substance_oel table; IOELV + OSHA PEL + NIOSH REL, never ACGIH)
//   §9 fire trio  -> Step-1 import (LEL/UEL + autoignition columns; flash_point already live)
//   §12 ecology   -> eco import (lc50_fish / ec50_daphnia / ec50_algae — live-wired below, > 0 guard)
//   §15 regulatory-> Step-4 import (substance_regulatory_status: SVHC, Seveso, TSCA/DSL, precursor flags)
//   EUH codes     -> ✅ imported session 10 (euh_codes on 148 substances, in-force ATP-state;
//                    ECHA ATP23 export with 2027 changes excluded — see euh_import_v1.sql)
//   §14 tunnel/LQ -> tunnel-letter + LQ import (dg tunnel_code holds the KEMLER number, not the letter)
